# BHOOMI-NETRA Citizen — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values from your Supabase project settings
# (Project Settings → API). `.env` is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix, and what it costs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expo only inlines variables with this prefix into the client bundle, and it
# inlines them as plain text. The Expo docs are blunt about the consequence:
# these values "will be visible in plain-text in your compiled application".
# Anyone who downloads the APK can read both lines below.
#
# That is acceptable for exactly these two values and nothing else. A Supabase
# anon key is designed to be public; row level security is what protects the
# data, and 006_citizen_tables.sql grants the anon role SELECT on shelters, risk
# zones and routes and nothing more.
#
# Never put a service role key, a database password or an SMS gateway credential
# in this file. There is no EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable that is private, so anything
# that must stay secret belongs behind an Edge Function instead.
#
# One more Expo constraint worth knowing before you rename anything: these are
# read in src/services/supabase.ts as static `process.env.NAME` property
# accesses, because that is the only form the transform recognises. Bracket
# access and destructuring silently produce `undefined` in a release build.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
